    {
        "id": "159987c13cdbe933",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "4f3052c660d65a97",
        "g": "6bceb4a7934b24fc",
        "name": "config flow",
        "info": "# Configuration Flow\nConfiguration flow for settings and debugging of entered config.\n\n## Information Input\nThe following information set needs to be set as \"flow\" variables to be available within the complete workflow.\n\n1. UUID for cycle start event at machine\n2. UUID for cycle end event at machine\n\n## Debug Flow Config\nGeneral function to get a debug notification, how the configuration flow is set up and which information set was entered there.",
        "x": 140,
        "y": 100,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
        "id": "b0d2ed4858f98d3a",
        "type": "function",
        "z": "4f3052c660d65a97",
        "g": "6bceb4a7934b24fc",
        "name": "Debug flow config",
        "func": "var flowKeys = { };\n\nvar payload = {\n    ICRRINUUID: flow.get('icrrun'),\n    DowntimeUUID: flow.get('downtime'),\n    machineName: flow.get('machineName'),\n    datapointConfigFilter: flow.get('datapointConfigFilter')\n};\n\nreturn { \n    payload: payload,\n    debugInfo: \"Added flow configuration\"\n};\n",
        "outputs": 1,
        "noerr": 0,
        "initialize": "",
        "finalize": "",
        "libs": [],
        "x": 950,
        "y": 140,
        "wires": [
            [
                "eef72ca0261a9eb9"
            ]
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": "69ba187a1f7d9885",
        "type": "function",
        "z": "4f3052c660d65a97",
        "g": "6bceb4a7934b24fc",
        "name": "set datapointConfigFilter",
        "func": "const uuids = [flow.get('icrrun')]\n\nflow.set(\"datapointConfigFilter\", uuids);\n\nreturn msg;",
        "outputs": 1,
        "noerr": 0,
        "initialize": "",
        "finalize": "",
        "libs": [],
        "x": 650,
        "y": 140,
        "wires": [
            [
                "b0d2ed4858f98d3a"
            ]
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": "45f88f75057fe6b9",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "4f3052c660d65a97",
        "g": "a34c93d53b1e1e7b",
        "name": "functional flow",
        "info": "# MQTT Connection and Transformation Flow\nConnection and Transformation flow to subscribe to MQTT machine topic and to decode, flatten and filter the data stream. \n\n## Information Input\nNecessary information to setup the connection to the MQTT stream:\n1. MQTT Topic of machine: e.g. \"datatroniq/waltershausen/h135/000-eba2-11\"\n\n## Process Flow:\n1. Subscribe to MQTT with known topic (or wildcard \"#\" to get topic)\n2. Decoding of Input Stream\n3. Payload generation and flatten to single messages\n4. UTC Timestamp in UNIX format for Messages added",
        "x": 150,
        "y": 280,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
        "id": "edbe797638f34e09",
        "type": "decode",
        "z": "4f3052c660d65a97",
        "g": "5f921015e3928c54",
        "name": "DecodeProto",
        "protofile": "070876cacf9b90c1",
        "protoType": "PLCPacketList",
        "x": 590,
        "y": 400,
        "wires": [
            [
                "0b2597bc7722b9ce"
            ]
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": "cfe49b800ec088b5",
        "type": "split",
        "z": "4f3052c660d65a97",
        "g": "5f921015e3928c54",
        "name": "flatten PLCPacket Array",
        "splt": "\\n",
        "spltType": "str",
        "arraySplt": 1,
        "arraySpltType": "len",
        "stream": false,
        "addname": "",
        "x": 1050,
        "y": 400,
        "wires": [
            [
                "2f68f137462e842b"
            ]
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": "2f68f137462e842b",
        "type": "function",
        "z": "4f3052c660d65a97",
        "g": "5f921015e3928c54",
        "name": "Convert sysTime (UTC timestamp)",
        "func": "var sysTime = msg.payload.sysTime\n\nconst seconds_epoch = Number(BigInt(sysTime) >> 32n) // keep only first four bytes (seconds since epoch = 1.1.1970)\nconst nanos = Number(BigInt(sysTime) & 0xFFFFFFFFn)  // keep only last four bytes\nconst millis = Math.round(nanos / 1e6)\nconst millis_epoch = seconds_epoch * 1000 + millis //this is UTC\n//const timestamp = new Date(millis_epoch) // this is most likely in UTC!\n\nmsg.payload.sysTime = millis_epoch\n\nreturn msg;",
        "outputs": 1,
        "noerr": 0,
        "initialize": "",
        "finalize": "",
        "libs": [],
        "x": 1360,
        "y": 400,
        "wires": [
            [
                "af0c5a8324b73dc9"
            ]
        ]
    },
